{
  "id": "measurements___absolute_vs__relative_frequencies",
  "title": "Measurements - Absolute vs. Relative Frequencies",
  "description": "Absolute and relative measurements to characterize and compare data sets. Calculate absolute frequencies, relative frequencies, and analyze measurement data.",
  "type": "calculator-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Measurements - Absolute vs. Relative Frequencies\n\nAbsolute and relative measurements to characterize and compare data sets.\n\nMeasurements are important in all production processes to achieve required quality.\n\n### Sample Measurement Data\nExample weight samples of a product:\n\n| Sample No. | Sample Value (x) |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | 1.0 |\n| 2 | 1.1 |\n| 3 | 0.9 |\n| 4 | 1.0 |\n| 5 | 1.0 |\n| 6 | 0.9 |\n| 7 | 1.1 |\n| 8 | 1.0 |\n| 9 | 1.1 |\n\n### Key Concepts\n\n**Absolute Frequency (h):** The count of how many times each value appears in the data set.\n\n**Data Set Size Formula:**\n\n_n = h₁ + h₂ + ... + hₖ = Σ hᵢ_\n\nWhere: n = number of samples, h = absolute frequency\n\n**Relative Frequency (f):**\n\n_fᵢ = hᵢ / n_\n\nWhere: fᵢ = relative frequency of sample\n\n**Sum of Relative Frequencies:**\n\n_Σ fᵢ = 1_"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "num_samples",
          "label": "Number of Samples (n)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 9,
          "unit": "samples"
        },
        {
          "id": "absolute_freq_1",
          "label": "Absolute Frequency Value 1 (h₁)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 2,
          "unit": "count"
        },
        {
          "id": "absolute_freq_2",
          "label": "Absolute Frequency Value 2 (h₂)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 4,
          "unit": "count"
        },
        {
          "id": "absolute_freq_3",
          "label": "Absolute Frequency Value 3 (h₃)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 3,
          "unit": "count"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "total_absolute_freq",
          "label": "Total Absolute Frequency (Σ h)",
          "formula": "inputs.absolute_freq_1 + inputs.absolute_freq_2 + inputs.absolute_freq_3",
          "unit": "count"
        },
        {
          "id": "relative_freq_1",
          "label": "Relative Frequency 1 (f₁)",
          "formula": "inputs.absolute_freq_1 / inputs.num_samples",
          "format": "decimal",
          "unit": "ratio"
        },
        {
          "id": "relative_freq_2",
          "label": "Relative Frequency 2 (f₂)",
          "formula": "inputs.absolute_freq_2 / inputs.num_samples",
          "format": "decimal",
          "unit": "ratio"
        },
        {
          "id": "relative_freq_3",
          "label": "Relative Frequency 3 (f₃)",
          "formula": "inputs.absolute_freq_3 / inputs.num_samples",
          "format": "decimal",
          "unit": "ratio"
        },
        {
          "id": "sum_relative_freq",
          "label": "Sum of Relative Frequencies (Σ f)",
          "formula": "(inputs.absolute_freq_1 / inputs.num_samples) + (inputs.absolute_freq_2 / inputs.num_samples) + (inputs.absolute_freq_3 / inputs.num_samples)",
          "format": "decimal",
          "unit": "ratio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Sample Value (x)",
        "Absolute Frequency (h)",
        "Relative Frequency (f)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "0.9",
          2,
          "0.22"
        ],
        [
          "1.0",
          4,
          "0.44"
        ],
        [
          "1.1",
          3,
          "0.33"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}